%[text] ## Simulink Copilot
%[text] Simulink Copilot provides generative AI-powered capabilities into Simulink and Model-Based Design. Powered by the GPT-5 mini model, Simulink Copilot helps you understand Simulink models, diagnose errors, get advice, and automate tasks. This GPT model may change as updates come along.
%[text] ![Warning symbol](text:image:2035) **Warning**. To use Simulink Copilot, it requires MATLAB version **2026a** or later. It is also currently unavailable in **MATLAB Online**.
%[text] ### Capabilities
%[text] Simulink Copilot is a recent update to the suite of GenAI capabilities within the MATLAB environment. As of 2026a, Simulink Copilot has a defined set of ways you can interact with it:
%[text:table]
%[text] | <p align="center">**Feature**</p> | <p align="center">**Description**</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text] | <p align="center">Explore</p> | <p align="center">Find tools in Simulink for your modeling workflow</p> |
%[text] | <p align="center">Understand</p> | <p align="center">Learn about a model or its blocks using chat</p> |
%[text] | <p align="center">Search</p> | <p align="center">Find and follow elements in a model</p> |
%[text] | <p align="center">Consult</p> | <p align="center">Get guidance on improving your model</p> |
%[text] | <p align="center">Troubleshoot</p> | <p align="center">Diagnose and fix modeling errors with suggestions</p> |
%[text:table]
%[text] 
%[text] %[text:anchor:TMP_690c] You can find the Simulink Copilot interaction in the Simulink Model Toolstrip with the following icon:
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Simulink Copilot Location](text:image:1f99)
%[text] ### Interacting with Simulink Copilot
%[text] When you provide a prompt to Copilot, it can breakdown the Simulink model into a set of different topics such as:
%[text] - High-level purpose
%[text] - Core components and roles
%[text] - Important block parameter highlights
%[text] - Simulation/solver notes
%[text] - Typical uses/experiments this model supports
%[text] - Warnings and practical checks
%[text] - Quick navigation pointers
%[text] - Follow-up Prompts \
%[text] ![Try this icon](text:image:807f) **Try**. Open the example Simulink model with the button below. Use the following example prompt in **Simulink Copilot** to tell you about the model:
%[text] ```
%[text] Explain the functionality and purpose of this model.
%[text] ```
  %[control:button:8325]{"position":[1,2]}

% Open sample model
open("SampleModel.slx");
%%
%[text] ![Exercise icon](text:image:0c3c) **Exercise 3.** Based on Simulink Copilot's output, what is the most appropriate explanation of this model?
ExerciseSol3("A model for learning how valve position affects tank level, volume, and flow/pressure dynamics."); %[control:dropdown:0bc8]{"position":[14,111]}
%%
%[text] ## Considerations
%[text] When dealing with LLMs, including Copilot, it is important to understand that you may not get the same output every time, even if you ask the same questions repeatedly. Because of this, here are a few ways to not only get closer to the result you want, but also help the LLM learn for future interactions:
%[text] - Ask follow up questions
%[text]     - Copilot is designed to have conversations, so make use of it!
%[text] - Verify the output
%[text]     - Run the resulting code that was generated to see if it provides the output you expect.
%[text] - Turn limitations into strengths
%[text]     - Try the same question again but with different wording if the code generated does not work.
%[text] - Use clear context and instructions
%[text]     - This is the best way to use Copilot. The more specific, the better.
%[text] - Clear the chat history
%[text]     - This will start a fresh chat. This helps when running into <u>**pitfalls**</u>. \
%[text] A pitfall in the context of LLMs refers to common mistakes or limitations that occur during usage of the tool. Common pitfalls that a user can run into with Copilot (or LLMs in general) are:
%[text] - Asking for too much in one prompt
%[text]     - **Suggestion**: Break up the tasks into smalls steps (piecewise approach)
%[text] - Seeing Hallucinations
%[text]     - **Suggestion**: Verify code suggestions in documentation
%[text] - Getting stuck in a conversation (repeated mistakes)
%[text]     - **Suggestion**: Clear the chat history and start over \
%%
